  "worked_solution": "We are given the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+2y=5 \\\\ x-3y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct ${D}_{y}$ we replace the second column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, according to Cramer's rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D}=\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
